/*
 *  bt_device_icons.r  --  per-kind 16x16 device icons for the control panel's list.
 *
 *  GENERATED by cpanel/scripts/icon-family-to-r.py from the artwork the user supplied
 *  as BluetoothIcons.sit. Do not hand-edit; regenerate if the artwork changes. The
 *  source resource fork is archived beside this file as BluetoothIcons.rsrc.fork so
 *  a regeneration never depends on the Pi share being mounted.
 *
 *  ⚠ THE TWO GENERATORS DO DIFFERENT THINGS, and they used to share the name
 *  "icons-to-r.py" -- the same collision that made this panel ship a stale MacBinary
 *  CRC for about twenty revisions under two scripts both named set-custom-icon.py.
 *  They are now named for what they do:
 *      cpanel/scripts/icon-family-to-r.py  every family, at its REAL id  <- this file
 *      scripts/custom-icon-to-r.py         ONE family, hardcoded to -16455
 *  Asking the second one for numbered icons yields a single -16455 family and no
 *  error at all, which is why the names had to change rather than be remembered.
 *
 *  Rez cannot `read` these types -- the same trap the CPU Temp CSM hit with PICT,
 *  where the `read` form is a silent no-op -- so the bytes are inline hex.
 *
 *  ⚠ Rez #include dependencies are NOT tracked by CMake. This file is wired into
 *  Bluetooth_APPL's DEPENDS via the stamp target in cpanel/CMakeLists.txt; without
 *  that, changing the artwork leaves Rez skipped and the build keeps stamping the
 *  OLD icons with no error at all.
 *
 *  ID MAP -- must stay in step with IconForCoD() in bt_panel.c:
 *      200  generic Bluetooth   fallback, and any row with no CoD
 *      201  keyboard            major 5, minor 0x10
 *      202  mouse               major 5, minor 0x20
 *      203  phone               major 2
 *      204  computer            major 1
 *      205  headphones/audio    major 4
 *
 *  ⚠ THESE ARE 16x16 ONLY (ics#/ics4/ics8). There are deliberately no ICN#/icl4/icl8
 *  at these IDs: the list rows are 16x16, and the panel's OWN file icon is a separate
 *  full family at ID 128 in bt_icon.r. PlotIconID picks the small icons from the size
 *  of the destination rect, so a 16x16 rect never asks for the large ones -- but
 *  IconForCoD's caller still checks PlotIconID's result and falls back to 128, so a
 *  missing family degrades to the old single glyph rather than to a blank row.
 */

